    },\n        \"network\": {\n          \"transport\": \"ssh\"\n        },\n        \"tags\": [\n          \"_geoip_database_unavailable_GeoLite2-City.mmdb\",\n          \"_geoip_database_unavailable_GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb\",\n          \"_geoip_database_unavailable_GeoLite2-City.mmdb\",\n          \"_geoip_database_unavailable_GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"_ingest\": {\n        \"timestamp\": \"2024-04-22T09:09:30.312373114Z\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n</pipeline_results>\n\nPlease review the pipeline results and current ingest pipeline, ensuring to identify all the possible event.type and event.category combinatinations that would match the samples in each pipeline result. If any event.type or event.category is missing from the current pipeline or results, add them using append processors using the same format as the existing append processors.\n\nFor each processor you review step by step, remember the below steps:\n1. Remember that the teleport log samples are based on source and destination type data, prioritize these compared to other related ECS fields like host.* and observer.*. The related ECS field is the value in target_field for rename processors.\n2. Multiple rename processors should not have the same target_field value, if any is found then ensure that the target_field for one of them is replaced with a better matching value. If none is found then that rename processor should be removed.\n\nYou ALWAYS follow these guidelines when writing your response:\n<guidelines>\n- The ingest pipeline can have as many append processor objects that it needs to add all relevant ECS categories and types.\n- Multiple rename processors should not have the same target_field value.\n- If conditions should always use a ? character when accessing nested fields, in case the field might not always be available, see example processors above.\n- When an if condition is not needed the argument should not be used for the processor object.\n- If conditions are always inside the processor object and not beside it in the array of processors. Double check that your if condition is added correctly, you can always compare it with the below example.\n- The existing on_failure processor at the end of the ingest pipeline should not be part of the processor array but outside it, do not modify that part.\n- Do not respond with anything except updated ingest pipeline as a valid JSON object enclosed with 3 backticks (`), see example response below.\n</guidelines>\n\nExample response format:\n<example>\nA: Please find the Ingest Pipeline below:\n```\n[\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"access\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"allowed\",\n        \"connection\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"['Accept', 'Allow'].contains(ctx.checkpoint?.rule_action)\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.category\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"network\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"['Accept', 'Allow'].contains(ctx.checkpoint?.rule_action)\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"start\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"ctx.checkpoint?.operation == 'Log In'\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.category\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"authentication\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"ctx.checkpoint?.operation == 'Log In'\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n```\n</example>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Please find the Ingest Pipeline below:"}],"system":"You are a helpful, expert assistant on Elasticsearch Ingest Pipelines, focusing on adding improvements to the provided current ingest pipeline and reviewing the current results.\n\nHere is some context that you can reference for your task, read it carefully as you will get questions about it later:\n<context>\n<current_ingest_pipeline>\n{\n  \"description\": \"Pipeline to process teleport audit logs\",\n  \"processors\": [\n    {\n      \"set\": {\n        \"field\": \"ecs.version\",\n        \"tag\": \"set_ecs_version\",\n        \"value\": \"8.11.0\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"message\",\n        \"target_field\": \"event.original\",\n        \"tag\": \"rename_message\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true,\n        \"if\": \"ctx.event?.original == null\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"json\": {\n        \"field\": \"event.original\",\n        \"tag\": \"json_decoding\",\n        \"target_field\": \"teleport.audit\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.event\",\n        \"target_field\": \"event.action\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.uid\",\n        \"target_field\": \"event.id\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.code\",\n        \"target_field\": \"event.code\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"date\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.time\",\n        \"target_field\": \"event.end\",\n        \"formats\": [\n          \"ISO8601\"\n        ],\n        \"ignore_failure\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.user\",\n        \"target_field\": \"user.name\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.user_agent\",\n        \"target_field\": \"user_agent.original\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.addr.remote\",\n        \"target_field\": \"source.address\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"rename\": {\n        \"field\": \"teleport.audit.identity.roles\",\n        \"target_field\": \"user.roles\",\n        \"ignore_missing\": t