ys inside the processor object and not beside it in the array of processors. Double check that your if condition is added correctly, you can always compare it with the below example.\n- The existing on_failure processor at the end of the ingest pipeline should not be part of the processor array but outside it, do not modify that part.\n- Do not respond with anything except updated ingest pipeline as a valid JSON object enclosed with 3 backticks (`), see example response below.\n</guidelines>\n\nExample response format:\n<example>\nA: Please find the Ingest Pipeline below:\n```\n[\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"access\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"allowed\",\n        \"connection\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"['Accept', 'Allow'].contains(ctx.checkpoint?.rule_action)\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.category\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"network\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"['Accept', 'Allow'].contains(ctx.checkpoint?.rule_action)\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.type\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"start\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"ctx.checkpoint?.operation == 'Log In'\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"append\": {\n      \"field\": \"event.category\",\n      \"value\": [\n        \"authentication\"\n      ],\n      \"if\": \"ctx.checkpoint?.operation == 'Log In'\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n```\n</example>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Please find the Ingest Pipeline below:"}],"system":"You are a helpful, expert assistant on Elasticsearch Ingest Pipelines, focusing on adding improvements to the provided current ingest pipeline and reviewing the current results.\n\nHere is some context that you can reference for your task, read it carefully as you will get questions about it later:\n<context>\n<current_ingest_pipeline>\n{\n  \"description\": \"Pipeline to process teleport aud